/** \file common.dox
 * \brief Scientist-facing guide to hciReduce's shared workflow and configuration.
 * \author Jared R. Males
 */

/** \addtogroup common_user_guide
 * @{
 *
 * Both applications use the same observation workflow: read FITS images, optionally coadd and preprocess them, run
 * the selected algorithm, derotate residuals, then combine and write FITS products.
 *
 * A configuration file contains sectioned `key=value` entries. Pass it explicitly with
 * `--config path/to/reduction.conf`; command-line options override values read from that file. Run either executable
 * with `--help` to see every accepted option and its current default. The
 * \ref common_configuration_dictionary "Common configuration dictionary" gives the CLI spelling, configuration
 * syntax, type, limits, and detailed behavior of every shared option.
 *
 * \section common_input Input images and masks
 *
 * Set `input.directory`, `input.prefix`, and `input.extension` to discover a FITS sequence, or set
 * `input.fileList` to use an explicit ordered list. `input.deleteFront`, `input.deleteBack`, and the
 * `input.qualityFile`/`input.qualityThreshold` pair provide reproducible frame rejection. Set
 * `input.thresholdOnly=true` to inspect the selected list without running a reduction.
 *
 * `input.angleKeyword`, `input.angleScale`, and `input.angleConstant` define the parallactic angle used for ADI
 * derotation. An optional binary `input.maskFile` uses zero for excluded detector pixels. A mask is part of the
 * scientific input: it affects preprocessing, local modeling, and final valid-pixel accounting.
 *
 * \section common_rdi Reference libraries
 *
 * `rdi.*` mirrors the input-file settings for a reference library. It is useful to algorithms that support Reference
 * Differential Imaging. `klipReduce` supports RDI; the initial `p4Reduce` implementation intentionally rejects RDI
 * configuration because P4 currently models target sequences only.
 *
 * \section common_preprocessing Coaddition and preprocessing
 *
 * `coadd.method` controls optional temporal coaddition. The `preProcess.*` settings control masking, radial-profile
 * subtraction, azimuthal/median/Gaussian unsharp masking, mean or median image subtraction, and pixel time-series
 * normalization. Use `preProcess.skip=true` for an already preprocessed sequence. `preProcess.only=true` writes any
 * requested preprocessed products and stops before the algorithm.
 *
 * \section common_adi ADI, fake companions, and final combination
 *
 * Both applications use the configured detector angles to derotate residual images before final combination unless
 * `combine.noDerotate=true`. `adi.postMedSub` applies a median subtraction immediately before derotation. The
 * `fake.*` settings inject calibrated artificial companions for throughput experiments. `combine.method` selects the
 * final mean, median, weighted, or sigma-clipped (`sigmaMean`) combination; `combine.minGoodFract` determines when insufficient
 * valid samples produce an invalid output pixel.
 *
 * \section common_output Output products
 *
 * `output.directory` selects the destination. With `output.exactFName=false`, `output.fileName` is a literal prefix
 * and hciReduce appends the next unused four-digit sequence number and `.fits`; with `true`, it is the exact output
 * filename. `output.outputPSFSub=true` additionally writes the residual-image cube. FITS headers record the
 * configured algorithm and final-processing provenance.
 *
 * @}
 */
